Case 3: benzene, three polygons                                                 
  3 polygons.
Timestep =   0.50 years.  Simulation length =   30.00 years.
Printout every   5.00 years.  Vertical profile stored every  15.00 years.
Koc =      60.000    ml/g,      0.21189E-02cu.ft./g
Kh =     0.22000     (dimensionless).
Aqueous solubility =     1790.0     mg/l,      50.687     g/cu.ft
Free air diffusion coefficient = .76000     sq. m/day,  2986.0     sq.ft./yr


Polygon   1
Sand                                                                            
Polygon area =      5000.0    sq. ft.
 20 cells, each cell  1.000 ft. thick.
Soil Properties:
 Bulk density =     1.6500    g/ml,       46723.    g/cu.ft.
 Porosity = 0.3800 Volumetric water content = 0.1200
 Organic carbon content = 0.00100000
Recharge Rate = 2.00000000 ft/yr
Conc. in recharge water =      0.0000    mg/l,       0.0000    g/cu.ft
Atmospheric concentration =      0.0000    mg/l,       0.0000    g/cu.ft
Water table has a fixed concentration of      0.0000    mg/l,       0.0000    g/cu.ft.
   with respect to gas diffusion.


